# Packaging attributes for the TacoTip Extras companion package.
#
# TacoTip Extras is a separate CurseForge project with its own package, so it
# needs its own rules about what that package contains. The repository root's
# .gitattributes marks `/TacoTip_Extras/** export-ignore`, because a TacoTip
# archive must never carry a second .toc.
#
# The two rules do not conflict, because they are read in different scopes:
#
#   * A TacoTip archive is built from the repository root, so the paths are
#     repository-relative and the root .gitattributes applies: the whole Extras
#     subtree stays out of it.
#   * An Extras archive is built from the subtree itself
#     (`git archive HEAD:TacoTip_Extras`), so the paths are relative to the
#     subtree and the root rule -- which names the `TacoTip_Extras/` prefix --
#     does not match. Only the rules below apply to it.
#
# `Tools/verify_release_extras.sh` builds the Extras archive that way, prints
# its file listing, and checks the package is the runtime add-on and nothing
# else. This file is the single place that decides what an Extras package
# contains.
#
# Note: in an attributes file a directory pattern does not recurse, so
# directories use `path/**`, never `path/`.

# The attributes file itself -- packaging metadata, not runtime.
/.gitattributes export-ignore

# The offline harness. Not shipped, opt-in, and it needs a game-free Lua.
/Tests/** export-ignore

# Lint configuration for the development tree.
/.luacheckrc export-ignore

# Marketing screenshots. `tt-2.tga` is the icon the TOC points at
# (`## IconTexture`) and stays; no PNG is referenced by anything that ships.
/**.png export-ignore
